# Optional reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS in front of the BL-AI backend.
# Caddy for Windows: https://caddyserver.com/docs/install#windows  -  single
# binary, no IIS needed. Copy this file to Caddyfile next to caddy.exe and
# edit the two placeholders below.
#
# Run manually to test:   caddy.exe run --config Caddyfile
# Run at boot: a Task Scheduler task (Trigger: At startup, Action: caddy.exe
# run --config C:\caddy\Caddyfile, Run as: SYSTEM, "Run whether user is
# logged on or not")  -  caddy.exe is not service-aware on its own.
#
# If your org requires IIS instead, use IIS with the Application Request
# Routing (ARR) + URL Rewrite modules as a reverse proxy to
# http://127.0.0.1:8000, and terminate TLS in IIS as usual; see
# docs/WINDOWS_DEPLOYMENT.md for the outline.

bl-ai.your-internal-domain.example {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}

# After switching to HTTPS at the proxy, set COOKIE_SECURE=1 in backend\.env
# and restart the BLAIBackend service  -  browsers drop Secure cookies over
# plain HTTP, so this must stay off until TLS is actually in front of it.
